{
  "id": "PA-HB-1114-2025",
  "scope": "state:pa",
  "title": "HB1114 (2025-2026 Regular Session): In inchoate crimes, prohibiting the possession of firearm at polling place.",
  "urls": [
    "https://www.palegis.us/legislation/bills/2025/hb1114",
    "https://www.palegis.us/legislation/bills/text/PDF/2025/0/HB1114/PN1236"
  ],
  "version": "as-filed",
  "operative_text": "Sec. 1 (adding 18 Pa.C.S. 914(a)): Except as provided under subsections (c) and (d)(2), a person commits an offense if the person: (1) knowingly possesses a firearm in any building, real property or parking area of a polling place holding an election;\nSec. 1 (adding 18 Pa.C.S. 914(b)): (1) An offense committed under subsection (a)(1) shall constitute a misdemeanor of the third degree.\nSec. 1 (adding 18 Pa.C.S. 914(c)): (3) The concealment of a firearm inside a vehicle by a person who: (i) possesses a valid and lawfully issued license to carry a firearm; and (ii) owns the firearm.\nSec. 1 (adding 18 Pa.C.S. 914(d)): (1) Notice of the provisions of subsections (a), (b) and (c) shall be posted conspicuously at each public entrance of a building where a polling place is located during an election.",
